If the save result is **not already announced** by a semantic update or live region, use this fallback from the window that initiated the save:

```dart
void announceSaveResult(BuildContext context, String localizedMessage) {
  if (!context.mounted ||
      !MediaQuery.supportsAnnounceOf(context)) {
    return;
  }

  SemanticsService.sendAnnouncement(
    View.of(context),
    localizedMessage,
    Directionality.of(context),
    assertiveness: Assertiveness.polite,
  );
}
```

After an asynchronous save, check that the context is still mounted, as above. Use a context belonging to the originating window; a global context could target the wrong view. `Directionality.of` preserves RTL support. Polite assertiveness affects web only.

Choose **one feedback path per save result**: semantic status/live region, or explicit announcement when necessary. The support check reports capability; it does not prevent duplicate feedback. Announce meaningful transitions once, rather than on every rebuild.

Verify saving independently in both windows, one announcement per result with TalkBack and supported desktop/web screen readers, and unchanged keyboard focus. Add semantics-enabled widget tests for the status changes.

